# The blog is a separate SPA bundle merged into dist/blog at build time
# (see the root "build:site" script). No catch-all "/* /index.html 200"
# here — Cloudflare Pages already serves the project's own root index.html
# for any unmatched path by default (verified: /about, /contact etc. hard-
# refresh fine with zero explicit rule), and an explicit rule for it hits
# the same "infinite loop" rejection described below for no benefit.
#
# Two Cloudflare Pages quirks shape every rule below, both confirmed via
# `wrangler pages dev --log-level debug` against this exact file (not just
# assumed from docs):
#
# 1. Redirects are checked before static assets, even for a file that
#    literally exists — so a catch-all "/blog/* -> .../shell 200" rule
#    would swallow /blog/assets/*.js, /blog/rss.xml and /blog/sitemap.xml
#    too. Those three passthroughs must come first and win by being more
#    specific (first match wins).
# 2. A rule whose destination is reducible (by stripping ".html" or
#    "/index") back to something the same rule's own source pattern
#    matches gets silently DROPPED as a false-positive "infinite loop" —
#    not just in local `wrangler pages dev`, this is also rejected at
#    real deploy time (Cloudflare error 10021). This is why the rule
#    doesn't point at .../index.html: any "index.html"-shaped target,
#    even renamed, also gets its own separate 308 "clean URL" redirect
#    back to the containing directory once served this way, which would
#    overwrite the browser's URL and break client-side routing for any
#    /blog/:slug. "spa.htm" (built by the root "build:site" script as a
#    byte-identical copy of blog's index.html, under a different name and
#    extension) sidesteps both: nothing here reduces back to a source
#    pattern, so no loop rejection, and Cloudflare's clean-URL redirect
#    is specific to the literal ".html" extension — ".htm" isn't rewritten
#    at all, while still being recognized for a correct, auto-inferred
#    "text/html" Content-Type (verified: no manual header override needed,
#    unlike an extensionless target, which serves as
#    application/octet-stream and — combined with the X-Content-Type-
#    Options: nosniff in _headers — silently refuses to render in a
#    browser).
/blog/assets/*       /blog/assets/:splat   200
/blog/rss.xml        /blog/rss.xml         200
/blog/sitemap.xml    /blog/sitemap.xml     200
/blog                /blog/spa.htm         200
/blog/:slug          /blog/spa.htm         200
/adr                 /blog/spa.htm         200
/adr/:slug           /blog/spa.htm         200
